<title>UK: Sema wins Thames Water contract.</title>
<headline>Sema wins Thames Water contract.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Franco-British electronics and computer services company Sema Group Plc said on Monday it had signed a seven-year contract worth over 23 million stg with Thames Water Plc.</p>
<p>Under the contract, Thames will transfer its mainframe processing and data centre operations to Sema as part of a restructuring of its IT department.</p>
<p>Sema also secured a contract to build a new integrated information system for French aircraft engine maker Snecma. The contract is worth 19 million stg and Snecma is investing 44 million stg in the overall programme.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
